    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed51fb1a_b25d6c0c",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/android/binder.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 306,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T23:11:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose I thought about the error information in an abstract way first before looking at current error scenarios. So these `ee-\u003ecodes` would be a way to uniquely identify errors and service them accordingly in userspace e.g.\n```\nif (ee-\u003ecode \u003d\u003d EE_RETRY)\n        retry_transaction();\n```\nSo, libbinder could retry the transaction regardless of the command or errno returned by the driver.\n\nThis would also allow _expanding_ into new errors if there is ever a need for it. Otherwise we are tied to current set of commands and errnos, or possibly parsing the string. We don\u0027t want to add `ee-\u003ecode` later on and break the api.\n\nI\u0027m not entirely convinced we\u0027ll need the `ee-\u003ecode` as I\u0027m not very familiar with binder errors in userspace yet. So I\u0027ll defer this to you, I can remove the code if you think is redundant.",
      "parentUuid": "42494ca5_9baf678a",
